# Shared API client

Canonical files: `@src/shared/api.ts`, `@src/shared/endpoints.ts`, `@src/shared/config.ts`.

There is no `customAxios.ts` — axios was removed after the backend moved in-process.

## Adding calls

1. Add the path constant in `endpoints.ts`
2. Base URL is same-origin `/api/v1` from `config.ts` (no `NEXT_PUBLIC_LAMBDA_URL` / localhost:8000 split)
3. Implement the helper in `api.ts` (or a focused sibling if the file grows)

## Current endpoints

- `COMPLETIONS` → `/chat/conversations/danny/completions` (streaming `fetch`)
- `CREATE_CONVERSATION` → `/chat/conversations`

Do not re-add Telegram or resume download helpers here; resume is static `/resume.pdf`.

## Transport

- Streaming completions: native `fetch` with `Accept: text/event-stream`, return a `ReadableStreamDefaultReader`
- Parse frames with `@/lib/parseCompletionStream` (`/&` delimiter, `data:` JSON) — keep chatbot and tests on that helper

## Types and payloads

- Keep request/response types next to API helpers (`Message`)
- Use snake_case field names that match the backend (`parent_id`, `context_type`, `context_id`, etc.)
- `context_type` (`"project" | "experience"`) + `context_id` (slug/id from `@src/shared/projects.ts` / `@src/shared/profile.ts`) are optional — set them via `useChat().openChat({ context })`, never construct a prompt client-side for contextual answers

## Config and secrets

- Browser-exposed values only via `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` when truly needed
- LLM and Mongo credentials stay server-only (Route Handlers / `src/server`)
- Never commit secrets into the repo
